.el .ds Aq '
.TH FATHOM_STATUS 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-status \- Who is keeping this index current, what it costs, and what is left (`e6.3`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom status\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-index\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIROOT\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Who is keeping this index current, what it costs, and what is left (`e6.3`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the report as one JSON line (machine contract `fathom.cli.status/1`)
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Ask the daemon at this endpoint instead of the derived one
.TP
\fB\-\-index\fR
Ask for a pass and wait for it, then report the state after it — the way to make `fathom status` mean "up to date" rather than "as of whenever"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIROOT\fR] [default: .]
The repository to report on
